%% CASE Northstar Insurance claims portal
Northstar Insurance is building a customer claims portal. Two Scrum teams work in two-week sprints; a document-scanning vendor processes paper claims.

| Data | Value |
|---|---|
| Remaining release backlog | 330 story points |
| Combined velocity (last five sprints) | between 50 and 60 points per sprint |
| Release deadline (set by a regulator) | 6 sprints from now |
| Escaped defects in the last three releases | 2, then 5, then 9 |

- The scanning vendor is paid a **fixed rate per scanned page**; volumes are hard to predict.
- Analytics show that **70%** of users use the "upload photo of damage" feature, while only **3%** use "chat with an adjuster".
@@ PR8 | Agile
What is a realistic forecast for completing the remaining release backlog?
A) Between 6 and 7 sprints, so the regulatory deadline is at risk
B) Exactly 6 sprints, so the deadline will certainly be met
C) Between 4 and 5 sprints, so the deadline is comfortable
D) Exactly 5.5 sprints, based on the team's average velocity alone
= A
? 330 / 60 = 5.5 sprints (best case) and 330 / 50 = 6.6 sprints (worst case), so 6–7 sprints. The deadline is at risk and scope priorities should be discussed now.

@@ PR7 | Agile
As the escaped defects rise, which cost of quality category is growing most directly?
A) External failure costs
B) Prevention costs
C) Appraisal costs
D) Internal failure costs
= A
? Escaped defects are found by customers after release, so their costs (support, rework, reputation) are external failure costs. Investing in prevention and appraisal reduces them.

@@ PR5 | Agile
How can the project manager best control the cost exposure of the per-page scanning contract?
A) Monitor volumes against forecasts and agree a not-to-exceed limit or review thresholds
B) Pay all invoices without review, since the rate per page is fixed in the contract
C) Convert the contract to firm fixed price for an unknown total number of pages
D) Ask the vendor to stop scanning whenever the project team believes the budget has been used
= A
? Unit-rate contracts expose the buyer to volume uncertainty; monitoring and agreed limits or thresholds keep costs under control.

@@ PR3 | Agile
How should the usage data influence the product owner's priorities?
A) Invest more in improving photo upload and reconsider further investment in chat
B) Invest equally in both features, since every feature is important to some users
C) Remove the photo upload feature, since it is already working well for most of its users
D) Ignore the data, since usage does not necessarily reflect a feature's value
= A
? Usage data is evidence of value. Focusing on high-use features and questioning low-use ones maximises value delivered.
%% END CASE

@@ PR1 | Predictive
A mining expansion's project management plan must include safety and environmental management. How should these be handled?
A) As subsidiary plans integrated into the project management plan
B) As separate documents owned by other departments, outside the plan
