A fixed price incentive fee contract has a target cost of $800,000, a target price of $880,000, a ceiling price of $960,000 and a buyer share ratio of 80%. What is the point of total assumption? (Answer in dollars.)
= $900,000
? PTA = (ceiling price − target price) / buyer share + target cost = (960,000 − 880,000) / 0.80 + 800,000 = 100,000 + 800,000 = $900,000.

