@@ PR9 | Agile
On a cumulative flow diagram, the band for "In review" is thin and stable, while the "Done" band rises steadily. What does this indicate?
A) Work is flowing smoothly through review
B) Review is a serious bottleneck in the workflow
C) The team has stopped completing work
D) Scope is shrinking rapidly
= A
? A thin, stable band means little work is waiting in that state; a steadily rising Done band shows consistent delivery.

@@ PR9 | Predictive
BAC = $4,000,000, EV = $1,000,000 and AC = $1,200,000. What percentage of the project's work is complete?
A) 25%
B) 20%
C) 30%
D) 83%
= A
? Percent complete = EV / BAC = 1,000,000 / 4,000,000 = 25%. AC is used for cost performance, not for measuring progress.

@@ PR9 | Hybrid | match
Match each flow measure with its definition.
1) Lead time
2) Cycle time
3) Throughput
4) Work in progress
A) Time from request to delivery
B) Time from start of work to completion
C) Number of items completed per time period
D) Number of items started but not yet finished
= 1-A, 2-B, 3-C, 4-D
? These measures, linked by Little's Law, describe the flow of work.

@@ PR10 | Predictive
A mining project must restore the site's landscape before the permit can be closed. When is the project complete?
A) After rehabilitation is completed and accepted by the authorities
B) When the last ore shipment leaves the site and the mine stops producing
C) When the project team is released to other projects
D) When the sponsor signs the final payment
= A
? Closure includes fulfilling all contractual, legal and regulatory obligations, such as site rehabilitation.

@@ PR10 | Agile
The final increment of the claims portal has been accepted, and the team will move to a new product. Twenty low-priority items remain in the backlog. What should happen to them?
A) Review them with the product owner, then hand them to the future owner or close them
B) Complete them in an extra sprint before the team is allowed to move to the new product
C) Delete them without discussion, since the release has already been accepted
D) Transfer them to the new product's backlog, since the same team will work on it
= A
? Remaining backlog items are reviewed with the product owner. They are either handed over to whoever owns the product next or closed, and the decision is documented.

@@ PR10 | Hybrid
A vendor delivered most of the contracted items, but two were cancelled by mutual agreement. How should the contract be closed?
A) Document the agreed changes, accept delivered items and settle payment
B) Close the contract as if all of the items had been delivered, since most of them were
C) Keep the contract open until the cancelled items are delivered
D) Pay the full contract price without documenting the cancellation
= A
? Contract closure reflects the actual agreed scope, with documented changes and settled payments.

@@ PR10 | Predictive
What is the main purpose of a final lessons learned session at project closure?
A) To capture knowledge that improves future projects and organisational assets
B) To identify the team members responsible for the project's problems
C) To approve the final payments to the contractors once their work has been reviewed
D) To decide the team members' next assignments
= A
? The session captures and transfers knowledge to the organisation; it is not about blame.

@@ PR10 | Predictive
Contract staff on a documentary production finish their work two weeks before the project closes. What should the project manager do?
A) Release them as planned, after confirming the handover of their work
B) Keep them until closure in case any further work is needed
C) Release them immediately without reviewing their work
D) Ask them to stay unpaid until the final report is approved
= A
? Resources are released when their work is done, as planned, after checking that their deliverables and knowledge have been handed over. Keeping them longer adds cost.

@@ PR10 | Agile | multi
Which two items should be in place before an agile product is transitioned to operations? (Choose two.)
A) An agreed support model with clear responsibilities
B) Documentation and knowledge transfer for the support team
C) A promise that the developers will fix everything forever
D) A new product backlog for unrelated work
E) A final velocity report for the operations team
= A, B
? A defined support model and knowledge transfer enable operations to sustain the product.
